From 8c6084fead2c8336155050edffb75b48de403170 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hoangvu12 <hggaming91@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 09:39:39 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] engine: child reports cover follow-up turns, thanks and
 handoffs

Real use of child reports (twenty parent chats over three days) found
where they went wrong, and this fixes each.

A child that ended its turn while its tests built, or with a timer or a
poll set, was reported finished, and the turn its runtime started on its
own later was lost: each message from the parent had one report of its
end. Now a later turn on the same message reports again, as a follow-up
keyed by its last answer, when it has something to say. A report says
what the child left running in its background, and the still-working
note lists a reported child whose background still runs.

A child that sent its result with send_message and then said it again as
its final reply was reported twice; the report now says the reply repeats
that message instead of the words. Parents thanked each report, and each
thanks woke the child for an "ok, stopping" that came back as another
report: report headers say no reply is needed, the instructions say
reports need no thanks and a child's result goes in its final reply, and
a short, tool-free answer to the parent's short thanks is kept in the
parent's ledger (-quiet) without waking its agent.

The still-working note no longer says "sent, not started" of a child on
another device whose copy here hasn't caught up (the row's last outcome
counts however stale), leaves out a chat the person has taken over,
names five children with how each stands and counts the rest, and only
names them when they're the ones its last note listed.

After a handoff, children kept reporting to the archived orchestrator,
and standalone chats kept waking their archived creator. An agent's
message to an archived chat (not its own child) is now refused, and a
child whose parent is archived or gone becomes the child of the next
parentless chat that writes to it. A result a create_chat(s) wait
returned isn't reported again, hours later or from another device.

A Stop an agent sends says which chat sent it, so another chat's Stop
isn't read as the person's; a turn Zeron cut off (a restart) says so
rather than "the person stopped it", and is reported failed when found
on the next start; a Stop the person sends before writing to the child
themselves says they stepped in. A report that came in after the person
stopped the parent sat in its paused queue until they wrote again; it now
wakes the parent, the person's own queued messages still paused. A
report too long is cut at a paragraph.

send_message asks a busy engine for its snapshots twice before giving
up, and says the message was not sent and is safe to retry.

Pi helpers reported "finished" with only an extension's toast for words
("fff path + grep mode enabled") when the provider had refused the
request. Pi's info toasts no longer go into the reply (warnings and
errors still do), and a turn whose last answer ends on an error reports
failed, with the error. Pi without a Zeron account was listed as signed
out, so agents thought they couldn't delegate to it; it runs on the
providers in its own settings, so it now reads as unknown, and connected.
