+A turn the child's runtime starts on its own after its report (woken by
+background work it left running, or a timer) reports again, opening with
+`(Follow-up: …)`. A report whose reply repeats what the child already sent its
+parent with `send_message` says so instead of the words. A short, tool-free
+answer to the parent's short thanks after a report is kept in the parent's
+ledger (`…-quiet`) and never read by its agent. A report that comes in after
+the person stopped the parent still wakes it; the person's own queued messages
+stay paused.
+
+An agent can't write to an archived chat other than its own child (refused:
+it would only wake it). A child whose parent is archived or gone becomes the
+child of the next chat with no parent of its own that writes to it, so after a
+handoff the new orchestrator hears its reports.
+
